! A square silicon sheet in vacuum with a PAW dataset: the cheapest cell that is
! both a two-dimensional material and an augmented one, so that a tunnelling
! geometry has somewhere legal to put its two planes. They go at 0.15 and 0.85
! and the atom sits at 0.5, which clears the dataset's 2.6 bohr augmentation
! sphere by 3.4 bohr. Bulk silicon cannot be used for this at all: its
! interplanar spacing along the stacking axis is 5.9 bohr with an atom every
! quarter of it, so no height clears the spheres and the guard refuses every
! one of them.
!
! The k-grid is 4 4 1 so that a two-cell ultracell at kgrid = (2, 4, 1) folds
! onto exactly it, and one division along the stacking axis is the
! transmission's own requirement rather than an economy: lateral momentum is
! conserved exactly and the perpendicular one is not.
!
! ecutrho is 4 ecutwfc explicitly, which is the only dual an ultracell accepts.
! Used by tests/regression/test_ultracell_augmented.py (PLAN.md P88 stage 7).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 6, celldm(1) = 5.5, celldm(3) = 2.5,
    nat = 1, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 80.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true., nbnd = 8,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'gaussian', degauss = 0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (crystal)
 Si 0.0 0.0 0.5
K_POINTS {automatic}
 4 4 1 0 0 0
